### Significance Tests

| Test | Statistic | p-value | σ | Interpretation |
|------|-----------|---------|---|----------------|
| Sign test (median vs 1.0) | p=0.628 | 0.628 | 0.48 | Median IS 1.0 — not different from balance |
| Overall binomial (50/50) | p=0.469 | 0.469 | 0.08 | Consistent with perfect 50/50 balance |
| Bootstrap balance excess (1,000) | 347 vs 305.9±9.7 random | <0.001 | 6.36σ | Highly significant excess of balanced superclusters |
| Bootstrap balance excess (10,000) | 347 vs 305.4±9.7 random | <0.0001 | >3.72σ | 0/10,000 random shuffles exceeded observed |
| Direct sigma from random mean | (347-305.4)/9.7 | — | **4.29σ** | Observed exceeds random mean by 4.29σ |
| Wilcoxon signed rank | centered on 1.0 | <0.0001 | 6.64σ | Distribution significantly centered on 1.0 |

**Key result: In 10,000 random shuffles the maximum balanced 
superclusters ever achieved was 342. The real universe shows 347. 
Zero random universes exceeded the observed balance.**

