## Physical Interpretation

The median supercluster maintains exactly equal disturbed and relaxed 
cluster populations. The real universe is more balanced than any of 
10,000 random universes tested.

**Possible conservation mechanism:**

Large scale structure self-regulates dynamical state. Within each 
supercluster, merger activity and relaxation occur at statistically 
equal rates. The cosmic web maintains thermodynamic equilibrium at the 
filament scale.

**Connection to dark energy:**

The ISW morphology signal (Parks 2026, main paper) exists precisely at 
z=[0.10,0.15) — the epoch of dark energy domination. The supercluster 
balance result spans z=0.01-0.80 with median ratio 1.000 throughout. 
Together these suggest dark energy may function as a dynamical 
equilibrium mechanism — not merely a geometric expansion term but a 
regulator of the merger/relaxation cycle within large scale structure.

If dark energy is a conservation mechanism, its equation of state w=-1 
(cosmological constant) represents the exact equilibrium value. 
Deviations from w=-1 would correspond to epochs or environments where 
the balance is broken.

**The physical picture:**

A supercluster filament has a fixed total mass budget. Dark energy sets 
the expansion rate which determines infall timescales. When merger 
activity exceeds relaxation, dark energy suppresses further infall by 
expanding the background, reducing the merger rate. When relaxation 
dominates, gravity drives new infall, triggering fresh mergers. Dark 
energy acts as the cosmic thermostat — maintaining the equilibrium 
between disruption and order at the supercluster scale.

